<section class="band alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="kicker">Read at your own depth</div>
      <h2>Everything an evaluator needs, at three levels of detail.</h2>
      <p>Technical buyers skim, scan, then dig. This page is structured so all three happen without a sales call.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="speeds">
      <div class="speed">
        <span class="tag">5 sec</span>
        <h4>The headline</h4>
        <p>1M decisions/hour at $0.04 per thousand. Calibrated, schema-valid, no hallucination. That's the whole pitch.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="speed">
        <span class="tag">30 sec</span>
        <h4>The shape of it</h4>
        <p>You define options at request time. Airmino returns one choice plus a confidence score and a machine-readable rationale code. Your systems act on it directly.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="speed">
        <span class="tag">3 min</span>
        <h4>The architecture</h4>
        <p>Calibration methodology, benchmark harness, failure modes, deployment topology, and the full comparison against prompted LLMs and rules engines.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .speeds {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .speed {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 26px;
    background: #fff;
    position: relative;
  }
  .speed .tag {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: #fff;
    padding: 3px 9px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .speed h4 {
    font-size: 16.5px;
    margin-bottom: 9px;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-weight: 680;
  }
  .speed p {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .speeds {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
